expression: "snap(ErrorKind::Tls\n{\n    host: \"git.internal.corp\".into(), cause:\n    \"invalid peer certificate: UnknownIssuer\".into(), looks_like_private_ca:\n    true,\n}, RequestCtx\n{\n    host: Some(\"git.internal.corp\".into()), method: Some(\"GET\".into()), path:\n    Some(\"/api/v1/user\".into()), ..RequestCtx::default()\n})"
---
error: TLS connection to git.internal.corp failed

  request: GET /api/v1/user
  host:    git.internal.corp
  cause:   invalid peer certificate: UnknownIssuer

what to do:
  this machine does not trust the server's certificate authority (CA).
  1. add the CA certificate to the system trust store, then retry
  2. or set the CA file for one command: SSL_CERT_FILE=/path/to/ca.pem fjo auth status
  note: use a trusted CA certificate. Disabling verification leaves the
        connection unverified.
